# What `moon package` / `moon publish` leave out of the published archive.
#
# This REPLACES the root `.gitignore` for packaging rather than adding to
# it: moon reads `.moonignore` in preference to `.gitignore` in the same
# directory, so every build output `.gitignore` keeps out of git has to be
# repeated here or it lands in the archive. Measured, not assumed — with
# only the three development-only paths at the bottom, the zip grew by 65
# entries, all of them `examples/moonbit-to-typescript/_build/**`. The
# other output patterns below never fired on the corpus as it stands and
# are carried so a regenerated `dist/` or glue directory cannot leak
# either.
#
# The bottom two are what `moon.mod`'s `options(exclude: ...)` carried
# until the toolchain deprecated that key: the fixture corpus and the
# TypeScript conformance submodule are neither of them part of the
# library.
#
# `src/cmd/tscheck` used to be a third entry, and it is gone because the
# path is: `tscheck` and `tsacc` became the `mtsc check` and
# `mtsc conformance` verbs, inside the published CLI's own package. So the
# two development entry points now SHIP, which is the one cost of the
# consolidation worth writing down — there is no longer a package
# boundary to exclude them at. They are inert unless invoked by name and
# add no dependency the compile path did not already link (`parser` and
# `checker` both arrive through `transform`).

# Build outputs and fetched dependencies
_build/
target
.mooncakes/
node_modules/
examples/**/dist/
examples/**/__tsmbt_glue__*/

# Development-only trees
fixtures
typescript
